05fc0f.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,3).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 true] [17592186314137 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/74850221ee168c6911ee5b6c319d2128f67149f81790528940822e253905fc0f.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,3).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 false] [17592186314224 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/6393810d90b8d340dbde041c43cb7e146cb59fedfcfd4a678827d291ea502b00.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,4]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,4).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 true] [17592186314224 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/6393810d90b8d340dbde041c43cb7e146cb59fedfcfd4a678827d291ea502b00.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,4]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,4).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 false] [17592186314231 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/029a51dccba9f1ec927c820fb8adb72e926b88a881f4646090ac651ef29da271.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on $(-5,3).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 true] [17592186314231 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041963/assets/029a51dccba9f1ec927c820fb8adb72e926b88a881f4646090ac651ef29da271.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on $(-5,3).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 false] [17592186381218 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381219 13194139536056 true] [17592186381218 1089 "q-125236" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381218 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381218 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/a7a36a62dcbbe0a0d67b9ccc8517eb7584e75d41d01227141229da3eed583500.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-3,4]$ and differentiable on $(-3,4).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-3,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381218 1113 #uuid "b24b1f9d-0768-54a7-a045-f1ebf26ee3d1" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381218 1145 "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following:\n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-3$ and $b=4.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(4)-f(-3)}{4-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-3)}{4+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-3,4)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{4}{7}.$*" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381220 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381221 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381222 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381223 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381224 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381224 13194139536056 true] [17592186381219 1110 #uuid "dcca2840-f4f8-5f50-b28d-ce12b2abd672" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381220 1034 "f(c)=\\frac{4}{7}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381220 1111 #uuid "f9834fc1-68ab-5c9f-98d1-9318078c44c4" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381221 1034 "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381221 1111 #uuid "0133ec9f-af36-5f92-a87d-38a6cbff465b" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381222 1034 "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{7}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381222 1111 #uuid "8f371631-8e29-5248-b657-ca3cc7123192" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381223 1034 "f(c)=0" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381223 1111 #uuid "f52e26a5-956a-5bea-893d-18bfc7eb0051" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381224 1034 "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{4}{7}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381224 1111 #uuid "3dd23e03-9c78-58d1-b589-b5dd93ff6c47" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381226 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1089 "q-125251" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$ on the interval $[4,16].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1113 #uuid "9c2ace5b-4a86-5d8b-a101-1aeed1dde583" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381225 1145 "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[4,16]$ and differentiable on $(4,16),$ hence, we can apply the Mean Value Theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (4,16)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=4$ and $b=16$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(16)-f(4)}{16-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(16)-{log}_{2}⁡(4)}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ c & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381227 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381228 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381229 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381230 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381231 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381231 13194139536056 true] [17592186381226 1110 #uuid "1d74fb0c-5981-5b86-a6a9-9ef17f6aad53" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381227 1034 "12" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381227 1111 #uuid "f0b611b5-e022-58ac-a112-ce62a70c2b8e" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381228 1034 "6" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381228 1111 #uuid "339c763a-b505-5cb6-94d0-384a3549bfe8" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381229 1034 "{log}_{2}⁡6" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381229 1111 #uuid "3fb8ec51-6a21-586a-abc8-f5f79feff775" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381230 1034 "\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381230 1111 #uuid "0a82503b-99f4-5f08-b0d6-950d392a1c2f" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381231 1034 "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381231 1111 #uuid "7799dac2-a0a3-5e9f-b2fe-9bb31e63aafb" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381233 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1089 "q-125252" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for $f(x)={log}_{3}⁡x$ on the interval $[9,81].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1113 #uuid "a95efa0b-db7f-50aa-a72c-805b5062f119" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381232 1145 "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[9,81]$ and differentiable on $(9,81),$ hence, we can apply the Mean Value Theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (9,81)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=9$ and $b=81$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(81)-f(9)}{81-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(81)-{log}_{3}⁡(9)}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ c & =\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381234 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381235 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381236 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381237 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381238 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381237 13194139536056 true] [17592186381233 1110 #uuid "50d2304d-ce4d-54fe-ba1d-b0010c6f58e9" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381234 1034 "\\frac{18}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381234 1111 #uuid "daa29262-3da5-53a0-a201-c2bfbbfde6ef" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381235 1034 "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381235 1111 #uuid "03aad5e8-ea9f-5fa6-a7cf-d1c1622aa435" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381236 1034 "\\frac{72}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381236 1111 #uuid "e19f8e8e-d058-5637-96ec-fc4a145adffb" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381237 1034 "\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381237 1111 #uuid "8bcd3579-8d58-5d07-99d3-f04035f5b57b" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381238 1034 "\\frac{36}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381238 1111 #uuid "995151b3-0f0f-5b7f-b59f-f4eed6526c09" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381240 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1089 "q-125259" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1100 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1]?$\n\n- $f(x)={e}^{x}$\n- $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$\n- $h(x)=x|x|$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1113 #uuid "3ad1bad3-5f71-5c57-b099-896ea09a9f40" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381239 1145 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1],$ the function must be continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|$ is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=x|x|$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-1,1]$ and differentiable on $(-1,1).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-1,1].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381241 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381242 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381243 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381244 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381245 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381242 13194139536056 true] [17592186381240 1110 #uuid "82df94f4-f1e3-59e5-a3a6-adc4cb378e67" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381241 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381241 1111 #uuid "2c61f722-e1db-5728-a3ab-366f444846c6" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381242 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381242 1111 #uuid "c2feb9d2-7956-5587-a890-0f3d1de73f62" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381243 1034 "I only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381243 1111 #uuid "b657eded-7b3e-5221-8420-0e617037df63" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381244 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381244 1111 #uuid "95fc7ad2-5d5b-544e-a288-831d6d1043ee" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381245 1034 "II only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381245 1111 #uuid "62c55912-e6e5-5ad3-9589-654044b75fc5" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381247 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1089 "q-127009" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1100 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-2,2]?$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1113 #uuid "225ac492-a1e7-5d42-8e19-52b35451f042" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381246 1145 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-2,2],$ the function must be continuous on $[-2,2]$ and differentiable on $(-2,2).$\n\nFirst, notice that the function $t(x)$ is continuous on $[-2,2]$ and differentiable on $(-2,2)$, so it satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nLet's check each of the other functions individually.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a vertical asymptote at $x=0.$  Hence, it is not continuous on $x=0.$ Therefore, $q(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $r(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=0.$ Hence, it is not continuous on $[-2,2].$ Therefore, $r(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0.$ Hence, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $p(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Hence, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$  Therefore, $p(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem." 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381248 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381249 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381250 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381251 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381252 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381248 13194139536056 true] [17592186381247 1110 #uuid "47fb4cef-55bd-5b8c-a091-6c6d42dabe4b" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381248 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/c30de46f9f22348af7a80c808ee8374fee195f44d3333c66c10803b42866a8cf.png" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536056 true] [17592186381248 1111 #uuid "1b18e931-00c3-5105-9ffc-fde99764b658" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381249 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/5f439fc57fa9cccf4471379d0b5a4901cdc4fd0ccd997fe9ae2e52d7c0372b94.png" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536056 true] [17592186381249 1111 #uuid "e15fc95e-f3f4-5585-b1ba-8bd6a58c8d70" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381250 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/83fffb6e46362e577cdc45bff6123555e070dc539505522ff134f2859954f9b2.png" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536056 true] [17592186381250 1111 #uuid "27424c7d-955b-50f9-be2d-6d0fc7550bff" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381251 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/2eba8ffb2094fab214cdebc0459ac6849c6bc2c37ac0f9bbd3fe026e44334800.png" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536056 true] [17592186381251 1111 #uuid "e6a0089f-a6a3-5e84-9576-a32315a63212" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381252 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/ffab62f3c9f42cd73ea6de5c9363de2218ba21fc0f53651c056494b47efc323a.png" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536056 true] [17592186381252 1111 #uuid "d6daffc5-fcf1-5c8a-b04a-e982c8883143" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381254 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1089 "q-2317" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1100 "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for  $f(x)={x}^{3}$ on the interval $[0,1].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1113 #uuid "8aa60ea3-4337-579e-bd3a-a287bb61ea84" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381253 1145 "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,1]$ and differentiable on $(0,1),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (0,1)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=0$ and $b=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(1)-f(0)}{1-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})=3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=3{c}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $c\\in (0,1)$, we discard the negative value, therefore $c=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381255 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381256 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381257 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381258 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381259 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381257 13194139536056 true] [17592186381254 1110 #uuid "ac508cf5-09b0-5ef4-b8e5-58e91c27a935" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381255 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381255 1111 #uuid "29947c6a-4526-5c3b-b860-95d1678c90df" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381256 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381256 1111 #uuid "1679c9c9-d05c-5963-bee8-c993282c6f09" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381257 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381257 1111 #uuid "a9bd7471-e64a-5857-9381-24b302e93a06" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381258 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381258 1111 #uuid "6d9e14f1-eaa2-5dbd-886b-f1d35503555c" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381259 1034 "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381259 1111 #uuid "567b304d-e1c6-554e-a029-d61730bc21ec" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381261 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1089 "q-345316" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1100 "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for  $f(x)={x}^{2}+1$ on the interval $[-1,3].$\n\n$c=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1113 #uuid "1627d046-23a7-5910-b67c-f60a8b23fe62" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381260 1145 "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,3]$ and differentiable on $(-1,3),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem.  \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (-1,3)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=-1$ and $b=3$ into the above gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-1)}{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{({3}^{2}+1)-((-1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-2}{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1)=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c & =2 \\\\ c & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381261 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381262 13194139536056 true] [17592186381261 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536056 true] [17592186381261 1041 "field-1" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381261 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381262 13194139536056 true] [17592186381261 1110 #uuid "ddda1bce-689e-5238-ba06-1b7f090e6042" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381262 1034 "1" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536056 true] [17592186381262 1111 #uuid "1df5aaa6-3a50-569b-b90f-432bb3994961" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381264 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1089 "q-48500" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1100 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3]?$\n\n- $g(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$\n- $s(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}$\n- $h(x)=x-2$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1113 #uuid "0c14a931-93db-572b-92db-617c82f326c6" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381263 1145 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3],$ the function must be continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$ is continuous and differentiable on $(0,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $s(x)=\\frac{1}{x-2}$ is not defined at $x=2$, so it is not continuous at $x=2$, which means it is not continuous on $[1,3].$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)=x-2$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it  is continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381265 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381266 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381267 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381268 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381269 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381266 13194139536056 true] [17592186381264 1110 #uuid "cacf94eb-033d-5913-9cb7-53c138e6a58e" 13194139536056 true] [17592186