sfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)=|{x}^{2}+1|$ is equivalent to $p(x)={x}^{2}+1,$ so it is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-2,2]$ and differentiable on $(-2,2).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-2,2]$ and differentiable on $(-2,2).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, the functions I, II, and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-2,2].$" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381272 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381273 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381274 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381275 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381276 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1041 "selection" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381275 13194139536056 true] [17592186381271 1110 #uuid "14836f09-3816-54d5-84c9-deca04cb032c" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381272 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381272 1111 #uuid "1177f855-7da3-5adb-b1cf-7ae26d427d69" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381273 1034 "I only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381273 1111 #uuid "13419a9a-43c1-5e94-a26d-003d8c5e5f25" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381274 1034 "III only" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536056 true] [17592186381274 1111 #uuid "9a54d50b-2e7b-5ec2-b9a7-21389e6d5259" 13194139536056 true] [17592186381275 1034 "I, II and III" 1